This result shows that the detrimental effect of an inclusion in a dual-phase steel is controlled not only by its absolute size, but also by its size relative to the surrounding microstructural features. For a fixed inclusion size, refining the martensite feature size can therefore increase the ratio  \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
